ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,E2A7EEDA47958B9AAEF5EE88AF2FACA7,"Approach your Town Center and register as a citizen.<br><br>The town keeps a chronicle of everything that happens <br> 1. Open Radial Menu at Town Center <br> 2. Select ""Register Yourself as Citizen"" <br><br> ONLY as a citizen you can build beacons. It is okay to switch between Cities, nor harm comes from that"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,F3A51A7840E017197FE118B2200EE279,"Bind a thrall to your settlement.<br><br>Every town is built by its people <br> 1. Open Radial Menu Town Center <br> 2. Select Manage Citizens <br> 3. Click on ""+"" Button in ""Register New Thrall"" row right under the Town Center Name <br> 4. Select a Thrall"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,0C73CF574F8408D30021039C237973AB,"Assign your thrall a bed of their own.<br><br>Citizens with a home sleep better - and work harder. Thralls get a positive or negative buff depending on their need <br> 1. Open Citizens UI <br> 2. Select a Thrall <br> 3. On the Detail screen select ""new"" in the Row for ""Bed"" <br> 4. Select a Bed <br><br> If you have trouble to find the right bed, try to change the name of the placeable by oben the ""Info"" UI from the mod. You can edit the custom name there"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,8F4C3A4A41AB37911DD6E2B9A4F23D1A,"Open the thralls schedule and set them to sleep.<br><br>Watch them walk home when night comes. <br> 1. Open Citizen UI <br> 2. Select on the left side, the Thrall selection the dropdown for Night. <br> 3. Select ""sleeping"""
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,D0BB290B49E5BE6044D557B9E1C29367,Set a thrall to training and choose your Training Beacon as their target. 
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,0B43E9CD46542A6AE0A8F090D17C5553,"Build and place an Idle Beacon - a place for your citizens to spend their off hours. <br><br> The Towncenter keeps track of all placeables, which have a smart component, be it vanilla or from another mod. Everytime you place a new asset you have to manually go to the Town Center and select in radial menu ""Add Vanilla Placeables"""
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,4BA719244EE2ABABF31C89A9BC51B64D,"Rename it.<br><br>The Restaurant, The Broken Mug - your town, your names. <br> 1. Open the ""Info"" UI via Radial menu <br> 2. Click on Edit Icon right next to the name <br> 3. Click on the name. You can now delete ""CUSTOM NAME""  and write your own name there <br> 4. Click accept"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,B35E7E954DE5D84FE0780E9AA304A020,"Place a few chairs nearby, then use Add Vanilla Placeables.<br><br>The town adopts them as seats. Seats are used by thralls to eat something, only if you have food nearby"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,0CF188C8431BE277788D7CB290044FB5,Build and place a food chest near the place you want them to eat
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,1A09373F4548DB488071CEA6AA2E559A,"Open the scheduler and make sure the needs checkbox is ticked - it lets citizens step away from work to eat and rest. <br><br> The needs checkbox is saved per Beacon. This means practically that you can have places where they can stop with whatever they do and then try to fullfil a need. If you dont like that because you only want to let them work or train then simply disable it. If in the next day part your Thrall is assigned to a different Beacon with needs enabled, then he will try to fulfill it then"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,2430D974484241F11D49E5A6DF634C42,Send your blacksmith to work the stall.<br><br>The stock is rolled when the shopkeeper takes the counter and restocks daily - what is on offer depends on their level. You can also hit Reroll to get another set of Items
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,9B8178374F30CD58800F7E8F11FC1AF1,"Open 'Manage Routes' from the radial menu of the Logistic Beacon.<br><br>1. Click '+ Add Stop' twice and pick a station for each stop.<br>2. At the first stop, add an action and set it to 'Load', then pick an item.<br>3. At the second stop, add an 'Unload' action for the same item.<br><br>Tip: if your item is not in the list, open the storage where the item resides once to let conan load it - the beacon can only offer items it has seen in the surrounding storages."
