ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Feed_4_Title,A Full Pantry
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Feed_5_Title,Care Enabled
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Feed_6_Title,Bread and Salt
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Feed_6_Desc,Stock the chest with food and watch a citizen sit down to eat.<br><br>A fed citizen is a living citizen.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Gather_1_Title,Mark the Land
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Gather_1_Desc,Build and place a Resource Beacon. It scans its surroundings and sets a daily cap for every resource it finds - your thralls work each resource until the cap is filled.<br><br>Do not forget: sleep and food greatly influence the daily outcome.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Gather_2_Title,A Place to Work
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Gather_2_Desc,"Build and place a workstation, for example a Wood Work Place.<br><br>Workstations mark where your thralls process a resource."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Gather_3_Title,Hands to Work
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Gather_3_Desc,Assign a thrall to the Resource Beacon and give them a work schedule.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Gather_4_Title,The Daily Grind
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Gather_4_Desc,"Let them work: your thralls walk out, gather and haul on their own.<br><br>Wait for the first yield to arrive in the Town Center storage."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Gather_5_Title,Reap the Rewards
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Gather_5_Desc,"While you are away, your town keeps working.<br><br>Select Get Resources in the Town Center radial menu to collect everything that was gathered offline."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Skill_1_Title,A Career Begins
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Skill_1_Desc,"Build and place a Work Beacon. It looks for vanilla workstations nearby - your thralls can work there.<br><br>While working, their skill grows: a blacksmith needs fewer resources, crafts faster - and his shop changes with his level."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Skill_2_Title,Man the Smithy
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Skill_2_Desc,Assign a thrall to a Work Beacon that has found a smithy.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Skill_3_Title,"Blacksmith, Rank One"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Skill_3_Desc,Let them work.<br><br>Wait until the thrall reaches Blacksmith level 1.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Skill_4_Title,A Shop of Their Own
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Skill_4_Desc,Build and place a Blacksmith Stall.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Skill_5_Title,Open for Business
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Log_1_Title,The Dispatcher's Post
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Log_1_Desc,Build and place a Logistic Beacon.<br><br>This is where a route is defined - one route per beacon.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Log_2_Title,Stations on the Line
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Log_2_Desc,Build and place at least 2 Logistic Stations.<br><br>Stations are where your hauler goes to work - each station reaches every storage nearby.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Log_3_Title,The First Route
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Sched_1_Title,A Place with a Purpose
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Sched_1_Desc,"Place a Worker Beacon next to a workstation such as a Blacksmith's Bench, then give it a name of its own.<br><br>1. Place the Worker Beacon close to the bench.<br>2. Open the 'Info' UI via the radial menu.<br>3. Click the edit icon next to the name and rename it to 'Local Smithy'.<br>4. Click accept.<br><br>The name is what you will pick from every dropdown later - so name it after the place, not after the thrall standing in it."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Sched_2_Title,Draft the Routine
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Sched_2_Desc,Open the radial menu of your beacon and select 'Open Scheduler'.<br><br>1. Click on 'Custom Routes'.<br>2. Click the '+' button in the top right corner.<br>3. Name the schedule 'Smithy'.<br>4. Select 'Smithy' in the dropdown.<br><br>A schedule is a named routine. One beacon can hold several of them.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Sched_3_Title,Hours at the Anvil
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Sched_3_Desc,"Add the Blacksmith's Bench as a target and set how long the thrall should stay there - 400 for example.<br><br>The time is counted in seconds, so 400 means the thrall works at that target for 400 seconds before moving on to the next one.<br><br>This is where a routine becomes a workday: add the furnace, the anvil and whatever else belongs to the trade, and your thrall walks the round in order."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Sched_4_Title,No Time for Breaks
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Sched_4_Desc,Deselect 'Allow Need Breaks'.<br><br>Every thrall working this schedule will now stay on the job instead of walking off to eat or sleep.<br><br>Use it where the work matters more than comfort - but remember that they still get hungry. Leave the option enabled on the schedules that follow and they will catch up on food and rest there.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Sched_5_Title,Put Them to Work
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ironlight-Core/IL_DT_JourneyStepsMerge.uexp,,IL_IL_Sched_5_Desc,"Assign a thrall to the schedule in the Citizen UI.<br><br>1. Select a thrall.<br>2. Scroll down in the details to the 'Work' section and select the beacon 'Local Smithy'.<br>3. Open the dropdown and change it to 'Schedule'.<br>4. A second dropdown appears - select 'Smithy'.<br><br>Now one place can hold different routines. Build a second schedule called 'Customer' with the spots where a visitor would stand, and your smithy has a shop floor as well as a forge."
