ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Feat_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Feat_Table_8691001_FeatName,Shemite Statues
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Feat_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Feat_Table_8691001_Description,XX_Desc: Shemite Statues
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693003_Name,Stag Statue
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693003_ShortDesc,Statue of a Stag
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693003_LongDesc,"Stately animal figures in varying poses represent one's wealth and prowess of claimed land. Shemite statues of the hyborian age are a result of influence from a mixture of Stygian, Kothian and Aquilonian cultures. This sculpture displays the mighty stag demonstrating lasting virility of Shemite culture."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693004_Name,Eagle Statue
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693004_ShortDesc,Statue of an Eagle
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693004_LongDesc,"Stately animal figures in varying poses represent one's wealth and prowess of claimed land. Shemite statues of the hyborian age are a result of influence from a mixture of Stygian, Kothian and Aquilonian cultures. In particular, eagles are revered as powerful spirits and their feathers and bones are considered sacred for various religious ceremonies. This sculpture symbolizes the regality and ferocity of Shemite culture."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693001_Name,Copper Ingot
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693001_ShortDesc,An ingot of copper
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693001_LongDesc,"The land of Shem is well known for its reserves of copper and gold. Copper being the more abundant and pragmatic material of choice for ornamental building pieces and sculptures within the Shemite City-States due to its malleable properties. Left exposed to the elements, it oxidizes to form a greenish patina called verdigris. "
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693001_FirstModifier,Ingredient
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693002_Name,Copper Ore
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693002_ShortDesc,A chunk of raw copper ore
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693002_LongDesc,"The land of Shem is well known for its reserves of copper and gold. Copper being the more abundant and pragmatic material of choice for ornamental building pieces and sculptures within the Shemite City-States due to its malleable properties. Left exposed to the elements, it oxidizes to form a greenish patina called verdigris. "
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693002_FirstModifier,Meltable
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693002_SecondModifier,Ingredient
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693005_Name,Ram Statue
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693005_ShortDesc,Statue of a Ram
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693005_LongDesc,"Stately animal figures in varying poses represent one's wealth and prowess of claimed land. Shemite statues of the hyborian age are a result of influence from a mixture of Stygian, Kothian and Aquilonian cultures. Rams are full of meaning and symbolism, often associated with fertility and agriculture in the lands of Shem. "
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693006_Name,Cougar Statue
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693006_ShortDesc,Statue of a Cougar
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693006_LongDesc,"Stately animal figures in varying poses represent one's wealth and prowess of claimed land. Shemite statues of the hyborian age are a result of influence from a mixture of Stygian, Kothian and Aquilonian cultures. The land of Shem has all manner of various creatures, but none quite as agile and stealthy as the fearsome cougar. Shemite culture reveres this wild cat as an intelligent and patient hunter symbolizing authority, balance and strength. Legends of old tell of certain Zuagir tribes catching and taming cubs to raise them as guards for their nomadic camps. "
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693007_Name,Raven Statue
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693007_ShortDesc,Statue of a Raven
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693007_LongDesc,"Stately animal figures in varying poses represent one's wealth and prowess of claimed land. Shemite statues of the hyborian age are a result of influence from a mixture of Stygian, Kothian and Aquilonian cultures. Shemite mythology shows the Raven with dual symbology. The Raven can symbolize wisdom and can be seen as a messenger from the gods signifying omens to come, but they are also known to be tricksters leading humans into precarious situations."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693008_Name,Cobra Statue
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693008_ShortDesc,Statue of a Cobra
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693008_LongDesc,"Stately animal figures in varying poses represent one's wealth and prowess of claimed land. Shemite statues of the hyborian age are a result of influence from a mixture of Stygian, Kothian and Aquilonian cultures. A relic when Shem was ruled over by the Stygians and their Setite religion, the Cobra was considered a sacred serpent of old by them symbolizing the strong, devourer of the weak and a powerful friend while at the same time a powerful enemy. Shemite mythology considers the cobra a protector adopted by city-state rulers as icons of their reign."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693009_Name,Sitting Wolf Statue
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693009_ShortDesc,Statue of a Sitting Wolf
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693009_LongDesc,"Stately animal figures in varying poses represent one's wealth and prowess of claimed land. Shemite statues of the hyborian age are a result of influence from a mixture of Stygian, Kothian and Aquilonian cultures. Shemite culture considers the wolf an essential part of the land symbolizing courage, loyalty and success at the hunt. Families in the land of Shem often keep small wolf fetishes in their homes for protection ascribed with both healing and hunting powers."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693010_Name,Howling Wolf Statue
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693010_ShortDesc,Statue of a Howling Wolf
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693010_LongDesc,"Stately animal figures in varying poses represent one's wealth and prowess of claimed land. Shemite statues of the hyborian age are a result of influence from a mixture of Stygian, Kothian and Aquilonian cultures. Shemite culture considers the wolf an essential part of the land symbolizing courage, loyalty and success at the hunt. Families in the land of Shem often keep small wolf fetishes in their homes for protection ascribed with both healing and hunting powers."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693011_Name,Dolphin Statue
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693011_ShortDesc,Statue of a Dolphin
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693011_LongDesc,"Stately animal figures in varying poses represent one's wealth and prowess of claimed land. Shemite statues of the hyborian age are a result of influence from a mixture of Stygian, Kothian and Aquilonian cultures. Shemite culture considers the wolf an essential part of the land symbolizing courage, loyalty and success at the hunt. Families in the land of Shem often keep small wolf fetishes in their homes for protection ascribed with both healing and hunting powers."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693012_Name,Dog Statue
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693012_ShortDesc,Statue of a Dog
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693012_LongDesc,"Stately animal figures in varying poses represent one's wealth and prowess of claimed land. Shemite statues of the hyborian age are a result of influence from a mixture of Stygian, Kothian and Aquilonian cultures. The city-states, towns and villages of Shem are full of the dog as an esteemed part of everyday life. Often seen in various roles working as protectors and hearders in agricultural capacities as well as family pets. It is said that even some of the gods are accompanied by them as regular companions."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693013_Name,Irukian City-State Banner
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693013_ShortDesc,Irukian City-State Banner
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693013_LongDesc,"Woven from fine silken fibers, this banner is decorated with intricate patterns that are seen in the central Iruk City-State district as an ornamental symbol of the region."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693014_Name,Irukian Well
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693014_ShortDesc,A water well similar to those seen in the City-State of Iruk
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693014_LongDesc,"Throughout the lands of Shem, water is considered a precious resource and an essential element for survival. Any permanent settlement near water will inevitably be contested by others who also seek access to this life affirming resource.The convenience of a well allows building in areas that would otherwise be unsustainable. Wells fill with water over time and can be used to quench thirst, replenish waterskins and perform the dozens of other activities that require the presence of water."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693015_Name,Irukian Foundation
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693015_ShortDesc,A square foundation made of cut stone blocks
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693015_LongDesc,"It is said that a building is only as good as its foundation. Foundations provide the essential stability to anything built atop them and prevent the growth of plants beneath them.Placing a foundation is a significant act in the Exiled Lands. Once a foundation is placed by a clan or individual, that land is considered their territory. Nobody else can build in the immediate area unless the foundation is destroyed.Cut stone masonry is a time-tested building material that is traced back generations – even to the time of Atlantis. It provides a sense of permanence and scale fortifying a base against all but the strongest of siege weapons or cunning invaders. The specific architectural style emulates the light-colored masonry found in the great Shemite City-State of Iruk."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693015_FirstModifier,Insulated
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693016_Name,Irukian Solid Wall
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693016_ShortDesc,A solid wall made of cut stone blocks
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693016_FirstModifier,Insulated
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693017_Name,Irukian Window Wall
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693017_ShortDesc,A solid window wall made of cut stone blocks
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693017_LongDesc,"Walls are a comfort for the timid, a strength to the strategist and a trap for the unwary.
A barrier against the savage world, walls can be built as high as the stability of the foundations will allow. The strength of the materials used in their construction will determine how long they stay up.
Just remember to add a door.
Reinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.
"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693017_FirstModifier,Insulated
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693018_Name,Irukian Doorway
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693018_ShortDesc,A solid doorway made of cut stone blocks
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693018_LongDesc,"Walls are a comfort for the timid, a strength to the strategist and a trap for the unwary.
A barrier against the savage world, walls can be built as high as the stability of the foundations will allow. The strength of the materials used in their construction will determine how long they stay up.
Just remember to add a door.
Reinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.
"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693018_FirstModifier,Insulated
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693019_Name,Irukian Stairs
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693019_ShortDesc,Stairs made of cut stone
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693019_LongDesc,"Any warrior with even a little battle hardening will agree that the safest ground to defend is the high ground. And if there is no high ground to defend, make it yourself.
Stairs are a necessity once buildings grow beyond a certain size. They provide points of natural defence and easy access to higher floors and rooftops (which make excellent archery platforms). Their only weakness is the material upon which they are built - if the high ground is brought crashing down then it no longer serves a tactical purpose.
Reinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.
"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693020_Name,Irukian Door
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693020_ShortDesc,A heavy reinforced door
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693020_LongDesc,"One of the strongest doors that can be crafted, the heavy door offers protection against everything but the most powerful of enemy tricks.
Raging hordes have been kept at bay by such doors and with a simple locking mechanism they become proof against incursions into structures.
"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693020_FirstModifier,Insulated
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693021_Name,Irukian Sloped Roof
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693021_ShortDesc,A sloped roof in the Irukian City-State style
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693021_LongDesc,"Sloped roofs are practical in any weather as water and loose debris are simply repelled running off of the roof rather than accumulating inside buildings. Built of close tight fitting metal and cut stone, this will provide a safe haven and strong front to any foes who come knocking."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693021_FirstModifier,Insulated
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693022_Name,Irukian Ceiling
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693022_ShortDesc,A ceiling made of metal and cut stone
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693022_LongDesc,"It is said that nobody is truly home until they have a roof over their head. Across the civilizations of Hyboria, rooves are made from a diverse number of materials - from clay-fired tiles warmned in the kilns of Agarapar to the roughly thatched rooves of the Nordheimers. In the Exiled Lands, however, materials are limited. Something to keep the sandstorms at bay and the bat demons from swooping down and snatching people while they sleep is probably good enough.Reinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693022_FirstModifier,Insulated
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693023_Name,Irukian Left Sloping Wall
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693023_ShortDesc,A sloped wall made of cut stone blocks
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693023_LongDesc,"It is said that nobody is truly home until they have a roof over their head. Across the civilizations of Hyboria, rooves are made from a diverse number of materials - from clay-fired tiles warmned in the kilns of Agarapar to the roughly thatched rooves of the Nordheimers. In the Exiled Lands, however, materials are limited. Something to keep the sandstorms at bay and the bat demons from swooping down and snatching people while they sleep is probably good enough.Reinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong."
