ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693047_FirstModifier,Insulated
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693048_Name,Irukian Crenellated Wall
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693048_ShortDesc,A crenellated wall made of cut stone blocks
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693048_LongDesc,"This crenellated wall is not designed to keep enemies out, but rather to provide defensive archers with a measure of cover between shots. Built of close fitting bricks of cut Stonebrick, reinforced by wooden slats that have been shaped to fit, this will provide a safe haven from the weather and strong front to any foes who come knocking."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693048_FirstModifier,Insulated
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693049_Name,Irukian Inverted Wall Arch
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693049_ShortDesc,A wall arch made of cut stone blocks
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693049_LongDesc,"It is said that nobody is truly home until they have a roof over their head. Across the civilizations of Hyboria, rooves are made from a diverse number of materials - from clay-fired tiles warmned in the kilns of Agarapar to the roughly thatched rooves of the Nordheimers. In the Exiled Lands, however, materials are limited. Something to keep the sandstorms at bay and the bat demons from swooping down and snatching people while they sleep is probably good enough.Reinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693049_FirstModifier,Insulated
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693050_Name,Irukian Ceiling Arch
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693050_ShortDesc,An arched ceiling made of metal and cut stone
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693050_LongDesc,"It is said that nobody is truly home until they have a roof over their head. Across the civilizations of Hyboria, rooves are made from a diverse number of materials - from clay-fired tiles warmned in the kilns of Agarapar to the roughly thatched rooves of the Nordheimers. In the Exiled Lands, however, materials are limited. Something to keep the sandstorms at bay and the bat demons from swooping down and snatching people while they sleep is probably good enough.Reinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693050_FirstModifier,Insulated
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693051_ShortDesc,Stairs made of cut stone
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Shemite_City_State/DT/Shemite_CS_Item_Table.uexp,,Shemite_CS_Item_Table_8693051_LongDesc,"Any warrior with even a little battle hardening will agree that the safest ground to defend is the high ground. And if there is no high ground to defend, make it yourself.
Stairs are a necessity once buildings grow beyond a certain size. They provide points of natural defence and easy access to higher floors and rooftops (which make excellent archery platforms). Their only weakness is the material upon which they are built - if the high ground is brought crashing down then it no longer serves a tactical purpose.
Reinforced Stone is one of the hardest building materials that can be created in the Exiled Lands. Weapons barely chip it and even explosive powder is not enough to weaken it in a single blow. Siege weapons or divine intervention are really the only way to bring down walls this strong.
"
