ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012402_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">Axes rose and fell above the plumed helmets, spears thrust upward, bringing down horses and riders.</> - The Hour of the Dragon

A weapon that combines the razor edge of the Great Sword with the momentum and weight of the Warhammer, the Great Axe is a vehicle of savagery and slaughter.

The brutish strength required to swing the weapon with any degree of accuracy means that the weapon is rarely wielded by commoners. More often it is reserved for the ceremonial guards of kings where it is used to convey power and presence.

In battle, a warrior who can control the weapon can create a whirlwind of steel around themselves, forcing their foes to stay at a distance or be torn to shreds."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012402_FirstModifier,Legendary
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012402_SecondModifier,Weapon
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012402_ThirdModifier,Sunder
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012402_FourthModifier,Frozen Paralysis
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012403_Name,Ymir's Attitude Adjuster
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012403_ShortDesc,A blessed and highly-advanced mace imbued with power of attitude adjustment.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012403_LongDesc,"While surface details concealed within the mace's construction hint at enhanced functions lost to time, godly imbued weapons are still unmatched at their primary purpose - mortal attitude adjustment. Capable of shattering bones through armor and crumpling helmets, the mace is a preferred weapon against heavily armored foes, bypassing the protection of their armor through sheer force."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012403_FirstModifier,Legendary
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012403_SecondModifier,Weapon
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012403_ThirdModifier,Shieldsmash
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012403_FourthModifier,Frozen Paralysis
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012404_Name,Ymir's Divining Rod
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012404_ShortDesc,A godly pike said to be capable of finding the weakness in any mortal.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012404_LongDesc,"It is said Ymir imbued this polearm with special properties to harness the power of the sky to help his devout followers uncover hidden earthly elements to better guide their path. However, Ymir quickly learned it could also find weakness in men's hearts to discover the chosen and infidels alike."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012404_FirstModifier,Legendary
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012404_SecondModifier,Weapon
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012404_ThirdModifier,Reach
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012404_FourthModifier,Frozen Paralysis
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012405_Name,Ymir's Stormshield
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012405_ShortDesc,A shield imbued with storm powers of Ymir.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012405_LongDesc,"The surface of this shield seems to glow with a strange luminescence hinting at the stormgod's power. Although lighter than a normal shield, it seems well fit for a frost giant's defense."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012405_FirstModifier,Legendary
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012405_SecondModifier,Shield
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012405_ThirdModifier,Shieldsmash
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012405_FourthModifier,Frozen Paralysis
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012406_Name,Tungsten Ore
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012406_ShortDesc,Greyish steel colored fragment of crystalline ore that can be melted with a catalyst to create a unique ingot.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012406_LongDesc,"This metal is unique for its toughness and has an unusually high melting point. It is typically found with other common minerals in nature. The raw ore can be combined with a catalyst to create special bars. Smelters and alchemists alike guard the secrets of the smelting process jealously, so experimentation with a furnace is required."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012406_FirstModifier,High Grade
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012406_SecondModifier,Meltable
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012406_ThirdModifier,Ingredient
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012407_Name,Tungsten Alloy
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012407_ShortDesc,An alloyed ingot created from cystalline tungsten ore
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012407_LongDesc,"This unique metal is quite rare in nature and usually found in small quantities with other minerals. It has mysterious properties coveted by the Acheronian metallurgists and sorcerers of old. Working with it was thought to be lost to time, but Argossean metallurgists found secret archeronian recipes to recreate it. It makes an excellent cutting material for weapons and tools due to its extremely high melting point making it harder than almost any other earthly metal. The base metal is very brittle, but when combined with argossean dream dust and brimstone it creates a ductile and workable ingot."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012407_FirstModifier,High Grade
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012407_SecondModifier,Lightweight
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012407_ThirdModifier,Ingredient
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012407_FourthModifier,Alloy
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012408_Name,Ymir's Ice Picks
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012408_ShortDesc,"A pair of short, icey sharp blades shaped from rare ice cystals. "
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012408_LongDesc,"Cut from large pieces of a rare ice crystal formation, the icey-faceted edges of Ymir's blessed weaponry open grievous wounds and cause extensive damage. These blessed daggers are a unique weapon, cold to the touch, but icey is the bite when used with passion by the gifted mortal. It is said the gods gifted mortals items imbued with special properties to only those worthy of weilding such power."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012408_FirstModifier,Legendary
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012408_SecondModifier,Weapon
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012408_ThirdModifier,Bleed
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012408_FourthModifier,Frozen Paralysis
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012409_Name,Aesirian Pick
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012409_ShortDesc,A pick made from Tungsten
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012409_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">The acolytes seemed to be following this thread, and there suddenly came to him Khemsa's cryptic words - 'Follow the golden vein!' On the brink, under his very hand as he crouched, he found it - a thin vein of sparkling gold running from an outcropping of ore to the edge and down, across the silvery floor.</> - The People of the Black Circle. The pick is one of the simplest tools known to man. Used extensively in mines across Hyboria to split rocks and gather raw materials.Tungsten is a rare metal, smelted from Aesirian and Cimmerian metallurgical recipes handed down throughout the ages. Tools made from this material are uniquely hard and extremely strong, able to break through the toughest of resources."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012409_FirstModifier,Supernatural
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012409_SecondModifier,Tool
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012410_Name,Aesirian  Pick-axe
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012410_ShortDesc,A Tungsten-forged combination of hatchet and pick
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012410_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">From his shoulders hung a loose black cloak, and over one shoulder he bore a heavy ax, the shape of which was that of neither tool nor weapon.</> - The Hour of the Dragon

A combination of hatchet and pick, the pickaxe is patterned off the peculiar tools used by the Afghuli tribes to break up the ice, stone and hardy trees that grow in their mountain ranges. The Afghuli may be considered uncivilized, but their wily cunning and resourcefulness has given them the ability to survive in one of the most inhospitable mountain ranges on the Thurian continent.

The Pickaxe can harvest wood and stone equally well and allows adventurers to focus on carrying more weapons and other tools."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012410_FirstModifier,Supernatural
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012410_SecondModifier,Tool
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012411_Name,Aesirian Hatchet
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012411_ShortDesc,A hatchet made from Tungsten
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012411_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic""> Then his manner changed again, with lightning-like abruptness; he recoiled with a startled curse, knife and hatchet flashing as they leaped to positions of defense. </> - The Black Stranger. One need only see the smoke curling from the chimneys of hamlets across the Thurian continent to understand the ubiquity of the humble hatchet. Gathering wood for cooking and construction are a part of daily life and the hatchet serves admirably for this purpose. Primarily used to hack down trees and fallen logs, hatchets can also be used in combat though they make unwieldy weapons.Tungsten is a rare metal, smelted from Aesirian and Cimmerian metallurgical recipes handed down throughout the ages. Tools made from this material are uniquely hard and extremely strong, able to break through the toughest of resources."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012411_FirstModifier,Supernatural
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012411_SecondModifier,Tool
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012412_Name,Aesirian Cleaver
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012412_ShortDesc,A cleaver made from Tungsten
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012412_LongDesc,"Hunters in the wild use whatever they have available to butcher their kills and the results are often less than perfect.

The cleaver, a tool perfected by butchers for slicing through flesh, muscle, ligaments and bone, allows the luxury of harvesting more useable flesh from every creature killed. And removing heads without damaging them.

Just don't try to use it as a weapon."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012412_FirstModifier,Supernatural
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012412_SecondModifier,Tool
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012412_ThirdModifier,Butchering
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012413_Name,Aesirian Sickle
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012413_ShortDesc,A sickle made from Tungsten
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012413_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">A long arm, which for the first time he noticed was armed with curving, sickle-like talons, swung high and swept down at his neck..</> - Beyond the Black River

Sickles are one-handed tools sporting a crescent shaped blade. Made for harvesting crops, such a tool can just as easily shear flesh and bone and reap a bloody bounty."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012413_FirstModifier,Supernatural
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012413_SecondModifier,Tool
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012414_Name,Aesirian Skinning Knife
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012414_ShortDesc,A skinning knife made from Tungsten
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012414_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">There's more than one way of skinning a panther.</> - Red Nails

Any warrior will tell you that a dagger balanced for battle is not designed to be used for skinning animals, though it will do in a pinch.
This skinning knife has a sharpened edge designed to easily split tendon, scrape flesh and free hides in a single piece. 

Using such a knife has the advantage of providing more hides with less effort."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012414_FirstModifier,Supernatural
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012414_SecondModifier,Tool
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012415_Name,Forge of Ymir
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012415_ShortDesc,The godly forge of Ymir
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012415_LongDesc,"A mighty frozen forge crafted with ingredients from the Frost Giant, Lord of Storm and War – Ymir. Legends tell of an Aesir blacksmith driven to obsession in his craft; ever reaching to create more powerful tools and weapons for his tribe. It is said that he finally reached the pinnacle by crafting a mighty axe used by a king of the Aesir to help drive the Hyborians and Vanir northward out of their lands. Although the blacksmith’s finely crafted axe was revered by the king, he was still unsatisfied with his work so he traveled north hearing of a myth that a forge existed in a temple made of ice which could create even greater weaponry. The blacksmith was never heard from again and tribal elders say he is still there at the temple’s forge drinking ale and making weapons for Ymir and the valiant warriors in Valhalla."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012416_Name,Heart of Remora
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012416_ShortDesc,The heart of the great ice wurm
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012416_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">When Conan awakens the next morning, he finds the girl missing. Following her trail outside, he encounters strange tracks and finally finds the remains of his horse and of Ilga, with the flesh sucked clean from their bones and the bones themselves surprisingly sheathed in ice. It is then that Conan recalls tribal tales of a creature named Remora, a vampiric worm creature whose body radiates cold and for which Ilga's ""Yakhmar"" must be another name.</> - The Lair of the Ice Worm, L. Sprague de Camp and Lin Carter, Conan of Cimmeria collection. This frozen heart of the great ice wurm is said to have been inserted into a wild white dragon many centuries ago by Ymir to create a unique beast loyal only to him. It is a rare and unusual item acquired only by the mightiest of warriors. Although strange, it must have some purpose."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012416_ThirdModifier,Ingredient
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012417_Name,Smilodon
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012417_ShortDesc,A summoned beast of Hyborian legend
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012417_LongDesc,"Hyborian legends are thick with tales of great beasts lurking in the frozen north. They are said to be spawns of the gods summoned to do their bidding. Stories tell of a mighty snow beast taking the form of a great sabretooth set upon the northern lands to wonder the endless icy wastes by Ymir to cull the heards of weakness, especially unworthy humans. It is said that this mystical beast devours all but the heads, which it brings back to Ymir as a gift. Occasionally, a great warrior encounters the legendary Smilodon and fights it to a stand still at which time Ymir grants the hero the beast as a mighty companion to assist the god in his battle of the demons from the outer dark."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/Ymirs_Respite/Data_Tables/ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite.uexp,,ItemTable_Ymirs_Respite_77012417_FirstModifier,Pet
