ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,ODO_ItemTable_Add_51816_Name,Phoenix-engraved Sword
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,ODO_ItemTable_Add_51816_ShortDesc,A broadsword carved with the symbol of the phoenix.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,ODO_ItemTable_Add_51816_LongDesc,"<LoreItalics>And as he stood, bewildered at the strangeness of his dream, he realized that he was gripping his sword in his hand. And his hair prickled at the nape of his neck, for on the broad blade was carven a symbol- the outline of a phoenix.</> - The Phoenix on the Sword

When the world was young, there was a great sage known as Epimetreus. Little is known of the shadowy past in which he fought with Set, the arch-demon, but it is known that for all the days of his life he strove against the worshippers, votaries and acolytes of the Old Serpent.

It is rumored that in times of need the ghost of Epimetreus flies on unseen wings to aid the kingdom of Aquilonia, and that the symbol of the phoenix belongs to the sage as much as it does to Mitra.

In any case, there is nothing to distinguish this sword from any other - save the glowing symbol of the phoenix carved into the blade.

<LoreItalics>Sacred Ablution: Your attacks can smite the target with 8 Radiant damage and attempt to purge up to 4 points of corruption from yourself or your target. If corruption is successfully purged, it deals an additional 3 Radiant damage to all nearby targets for each point of corruption removed. Attacks against evil-aligned targets are treated as if they always purged full corruption.</>

<LoreItalics>Radiant magic damage sometimes marks the target, causing them to take additional flat True damage when hit for a short while.</>

<LoreItalics>Adaptive weapons use your higher weapon damage attribute, Strength or Agility, and benefit from the matching bonus weapon damage stat on your armor.</>"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,ODO_ItemTable_Add_51816_FirstModifier,Hallowed
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,ODO_ItemTable_Add_51816_SecondModifier,Sacred Ablution
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,ODO_ItemTable_Add_47210076_Name,Phoenix-brand
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,ODO_ItemTable_Add_47210076_ShortDesc,A burning brand sanctified in the name of Mitra.
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,ODO_ItemTable_Add_47210076_LongDesc,"<LoreItalics>Mitra was not kind in the way soft gods are kind. His light promised judgment, cleansing, and the stern mercy of law; beneath it, corruption had no shadow deep enough to hide.</>

This torch is a sacred light carried by the faithful of Mitra.

<LoreItalics>Sacred Ablution: Your attacks can smite the target with 8 Radiant damage and attempt to purge up to 4 points of corruption from yourself or your target. If corruption is successfully purged, it deals an additional 3 Radiant damage to all nearby targets for each point of corruption removed. Attacks against evil-aligned targets are treated as if they always purged full corruption.</>

<LoreItalics>Radiant magic damage sometimes marks the target, causing them to take additional flat True damage when hit for a short while.</>

<LoreItalics>Adaptive weapons use your higher weapon damage attribute, Strength or Agility, and benefit from the matching bonus weapon damage stat on your armor.</>"
