ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,EoT_ItemTable_Merge_53658_ShortDesc,Arrows of sacred ice carrying Ymir's killing cold
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,EoT_ItemTable_Merge_53658_LongDesc,"<LoreItalics>Better if steel and bowstring prevail without further aid from the arts, for the constant use of mighty spells sometimes sets forces in motion that might rock the universe.</> - The Hour of the Dragon

These arrows are hewn from ice blessed in Ymir's name, carrying the killing cold of the north wherever they strike.

<LoreItalics>Ice Shard: Shots with these arrows deal Primal water damage instead of physical damage.</>

<LoreItalics>Primal magic damage sometimes puts a stacking damage-over-time debuff on your target that deals more Primal damage and can stack from its own damage. Each of the four elements stacks separately.</>"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,ODO_ItemTable_Add_53658_FirstModifier,Hallowed
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,ODO_ItemTable_Add_53658_SecondModifier,Deals Primal Damage
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,EoT_ItemTable_Add_47210136_Name,Shard of Notion
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,EoT_ItemTable_Add_47210136_ShortDesc,A fragment of something larger
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EraOfTrials/Systems/DataTables/Religion/EoT_DT_Religious_Item_Add.uexp,,EoT_ItemTable_Add_47210136_LongDesc,"This small chunk of rock bears a mark across one face, as if it's been broken off from something larger and more elaborate. Holding it gives you a sense that unseen truths await discovery.

<LoreItalics>Shards of Notion are fragments of divine insight gathered through acts of faith. Religious teachers may be interested in these fragments.</>"
