ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_51420_Name,Grey One Mask
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_51420_ShortDesc,A mask made to imitate the Grey One
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_51420_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">Conan mentally termed the creatures black men, for lack of a better term; instinctively he knew that these tall ebony beings were not men, as he understood the term..</> - Pool of the Black One

It is not known whence came the tall, alien beings known as the Grey Ones. Standing taller than any human, their diabolism is matched only by their raw strength. The inhabitats of the Isle of Siptah know well enough to maintain their distance from these strange beings - those careless enough to be caught simply vanish forever.

This mask is a gruesome attempt to mimic the face coverings worn by the Grey Ones. It is not as fear inducing as the presence of the creatures themselves, but it captures the eerie diabolism of their features."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_51420_FirstModifier,Light Armor
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52011_Name,Medium Cap
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52011_ShortDesc,A riveted leather cap with a facemask
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52011_LongDesc,"This leather helmet includes large cheek  and neck protectors and a facemask for filtering the sand and dust from the air.
Offering significantly more protection than light armor, this medium armor incorporates many elements - metal rivets, articulated leather, and fur-trimmed cloth to balance protection and agility. This middle of the road approach brings compromises of its own because this armor is neither as strong as heavy armor, nor as flexible as light armor.
This riveted armor bears no cultural markings or identifiers of any type."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52011_FirstModifier,Medium Armor
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_91005_Name,Medium Cap
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_91005_ShortDesc,A riveted leather cap with a facemask
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_91005_LongDesc,"This leather helmet includes large cheek  and neck protectors and a facemask for filtering the sand and dust from the air.
Offering significantly more protection than light armor, this medium armor incorporates many elements - metal rivets, articulated leather, and fur-trimmed cloth to balance protection and agility. This middle of the road approach brings compromises of its own because this armor is neither as strong as heavy armor, nor as flexible as light armor.
This riveted armor bears no cultural markings or identifiers of any type."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_91005_FirstModifier,Medium Armor
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52071_Name,Darfari Watcher Mask
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52071_ShortDesc,A ritual mask used by Darfari shamans to see the dead
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52071_LongDesc,"Carved into solid wood and decorated with intricate symbols, the watcher mask is said to remove the veil between the wearer and the spiritual world where Yog dwells.
Darfari slaves, captured and carried into the Hyborian kingdoms do not have shamans of their own, and are forced to practise a perverted version of their religion. They have long since lost the art of creating masks such as these.
But in the southern deserts, darfari shamans practise a purer version of the religion. Through the aid of these masks they can see the dead and, it is rumored, manifestations of Yog himself.

This mask offers some protection from both weapons and the elements."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52071_FirstModifier,Light Armor
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52076_Name,Darfari Speaker Mask
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52076_ShortDesc,A ritual mask used by Darfari shamans to see the dead
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52076_LongDesc,"Carved into solid wood and decorated with intricate symbols, the speaker mask is said to allow the wearer to communicate with the dead.
Darfari slaves, captured and carried into the Hyborian kingdoms do not have shamans of their own, and are forced to practise a perverted version of their religion. They have long since lost the art of creating masks such as these.
But in the southern deserts, darfari shamans practise a purer version of the religion. Through the aid of these masks they can command the dead and communicate with Yog directly."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52076_FirstModifier,Light Armor
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52541_Name,Relic Hunter Turban
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52541_ShortDesc,A turban designed to protect the head from the elements
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52541_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">He was a far traveler and had looted the treasures of many kingdoms. But now he hesitated and shuddered before the highest adventure and the mightiest treasure of all.</> - Black Colossus

The Relic Hunters of the Exiled Lands are a curious mix of mercenaries, thieves and desperate fools. They were the original group in the Exiled Lands, exhorted to come in search of great treasures in the ruins that dot the area.

The price of their admission was to wear a bracelet that ensured they could not run off with the treasures that they found.

This turban has been refined in the time that they have spent in the Exiled Lands, offering comfort against the warm weather of the region and limited protection against the scouring sands."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52541_FirstModifier,Light Armor
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_91040_Name,Relic Hunter Turban
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_91040_ShortDesc,A turban designed to protect the head from the elements
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_91040_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">He was a far traveler and had looted the treasures of many kingdoms. But now he hesitated and shuddered before the highest adventure and the mightiest treasure of all.</> - Black Colossus

The Relic Hunters of the Exiled Lands are a curious mix of mercenaries, thieves and desperate fools. They were the original group in the Exiled Lands, exhorted to come in search of great treasures in the ruins that dot the area.

The price of their admission was to wear a bracelet that ensured they could not run off with the treasures that they found.

This turban has been refined in the time that they have spent in the Exiled Lands, offering comfort against the warm weather of the region and limited protection against the scouring sands."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_91040_FirstModifier,Light Armor
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52603_Name,Silent Legion Helmet
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52603_ShortDesc,An ancient helmet with a ghastly aura
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52603_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">It is sorcery - grisly black magic from the grim youth of the world. An awful shape has risen out of the shades of the Past, and none can stand before it.</> - The Hour of the Dragon

This eldritch helm bears markings and script so old no living scholar could decipher them.

The pinnacle of protection, steel armor is a solid wall of defense against any type of attack, but the extreme weight requirements mean that the wearer must sacrifice mobility. 

The strange metal of this primordial armor always carries an unholy chill, even in the noonday sun. When donning this wicked carapace, the wearer hears whispering voices, voices that tell an ancient tragedy - voices that whisper the names Deathbringer, Kinscourge, and Maimer."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52603_FirstModifier,Heavy Armor
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52649_Name,Silent Legion Light Helmet
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52649_ShortDesc,An ancient helmet with a less-than ghastly aura
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52649_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">It is sorcery - grisly black magic from the grim youth of the world. An awful shape has risen out of the shades of the Past, and none can stand before it.</> - The Hour of the Dragon 

This eldritch helm bears markings and script so old no living scholar could decipher them. 

A lighter, inferior copy of the armor worn by Tyros the Deathbringer - one can forgive the smith for wanting to imitate such a superior set of armor. However, without the weight of sorrow and the unique experiences of Tyros and his life."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52649_FirstModifier,Light Armor
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52654_Name,Silent Legion Medium Helmet
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52654_ShortDesc,An ancient helmet with a less-than ghastly aura
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52654_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">It is sorcery - grisly black magic from the grim youth of the world. An awful shape has risen out of the shades of the Past, and none can stand before it.</> - The Hour of the Dragon 

This eldritch helm bears markings and script so old no living scholar could decipher them. 

Offering significantly more protection than light armor, this medium armor incorporates many elements - metal rivets, articulated leather, and fur-trimmed cloth - to balance protection and agility. This middle of the road approach brings compromises of its own because this armor is neither as strong as heavy armor, nor as flexible as light armor. 

An inferior copy of the armor worn by Tyros the Deathbringer - one can forgive the smith for wanting to imitate such a superior set of armor. However, without the weight of sorrow and the unique experiences of Tyros and his life."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52654_FirstModifier,Medium Armor
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52935_Name,Zamorian Thief Hood
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52935_ShortDesc,A hood for those who work in the shadows
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52935_LongDesc,"<span style=""italic"">Native rogues were the dominant element - dark-skinned, dark-eyed Zamorians, with daggers at their girdles and guile in their hearts.</> - The Tower of the Elephant

Among the shadow haunted streets of Shadizar and the wild, dangerous streets of The Maul, the dark-skinned Zamorian thieves work their stealthy trade.

Designed with the principle that the best fight is a fight avoided, this outfit allows the wearer to blend into the shadows and remain unseen in the deep shadows of the Zamorian cities. 
Whether it is as effective in the lands beyond Zamoria is another question."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_52935_FirstModifier,Light Armor
