This eldritch helm bears markings and script so old no living scholar could decipher them.

The pinnacle of protection, steel armor is a solid wall of defense against any type of attack, but the extreme weight requirements mean that the wearer must sacrifice mobility. 

The strange metal of this primordial armor always carries an unholy chill, even in the noonday sun. When donning this wicked carapace, the wearer hears whispering voices, voices that tell an ancient tragedy - voices that whisper the names Deathbringer, Kinscourge, and Maimer."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_91320_FirstModifier,Heavy Armor
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_51378_Name,Voidforged Dragon Helmet
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_51378_ShortDesc,A helmet taken from the Voidforge
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/SevereWeatherEnhanced/DataTables/LFS_ItemTable.uexp,,LFS_ItemTable_51378_LongDesc,"Inside the Tower of Siptah, on the first floor of the tower, is a place known as the Voidforge. Relics appear here, their origins drawn from across the cosmos. Where the veil between worlds is thinnest, these items are hammered into existence by the Voidforge. Sometimes something simple, sometimes something exotic. The Voidforge does not care for craftsmanship or flair - the rules that govern what appears within are unfathomable."
