ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/MoreKatanas/DataTables/MoreKatanas_ItemTable.uexp,,5A34A5D54E553FB631CBD59D5DCB1079,"Without proper 'steel folding' techniques the strength of this sword is questionable at best. The jagged edge is flecked with rust and bleeds the enemy with every strike, but any hard hit threatens to shatter it.

Even a crude weapon is better than none, but do not expect it to last long."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/MoreKatanas/DataTables/MoreKatanas_ItemTable.uexp,,1C0E1316437A74430EC0DB856E844902,Steel Katana
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/MoreKatanas/DataTables/MoreKatanas_ItemTable.uexp,,B72DA50049A490D66A2DDF91F6EF2028,A two-handed sword of Yamatai design
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/MoreKatanas/DataTables/MoreKatanas_ItemTable.uexp,,84A3185F42F5FACDD61A2498E75BF70D,"The people of Yamatai trade regularly along the eastern coastline of the Thurian continent - and their dhows can be seen docked from Vendhya and Kambuja to Paikang in Khitai. They have access to purer forms of metal on their volcanic islands than many of the cultures on the main continent. 

They have developed a process called 'steel folding' that allows them to create very strong, sharp blades with a high amount of metal purity. This type of smithing is a closely guarded secret and would not be willingly taught to strangers."
