ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_51556_Name,Eye of the Khan
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_51556_ShortDesc,A Hyrkanian bow with remarkable accuracy
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_51556_LongDesc,"Across the Vilayet, where the blue sea gives way to the steppes, the Hyrkanians live in the saddle from the day that they are born - learning to shoot, fight and eat.

This bow was crafted for the son of a great khan, but the boy was trampled by bulls before he was ten years old and the old khan was left with nothing but the bow in memory of his favored son.

The old khan claimed that the bow would whisper to him with the voice of his son, telling him where to find water and how to avoid enemies. The Khan's other sons saw this as a sign of their father being unfit to rule, and promptly knifed him in the back.

The bow was given away, or lost, or sold. And the son of the khan was forgotten."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_51556_FirstModifier,Legendary
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_51556_SecondModifier,Power Draw
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_50523_Name,Reach of the Red Mother
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_50523_ShortDesc,A bow crafted of exquisite dragonbone
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_50523_LongDesc,"<LoreItalics>And their magicians made a terrible magic to guard the city; for by their necromantic arts they re-created the dragons which had once dwelt in this lost land, and whose monstrous bones they found in the forest. Those bones they clothed in flesh and life, and the living beasts walked the earth as they walked it when time was young.</> - Red Nails

Through the long passage of eons, rumors of dragons have always been passed down from generation to generation, and the legacy of these fearsome creatures grows with each telling."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_50523_FirstModifier,Legendary
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_52614_ShortDesc,Boots that crunch like snow with every step
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_52614_LongDesc,"<LoreItalics>Above him the skies glowed and crackled with strange lights and gleams. The snow shone weirdly, now frosty blue, now icy crimson, now cold silver. Through a shimmering icy realm of enchantment Conan plunged doggedly onward, in a crystalline maze where the only reality was the white body dancing across the glittering snow beyond his reach - ever beyond his reach.</> - The Frost-Giant's Daughter

These boots of winter weirdness mark one as devout to Ymir, Father of Giants, Lord of Storm and War."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_52614_FirstModifier,Hallowed
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_52614_SecondModifier,Heavy
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_53651_LongDesc,"<LoreItalics>Better if steel and bowstring prevail without further aid from the arts, for the constant use of mighty spells sometimes sets forces in motion that might rock the universe.</> - The Hour of the Dragon

A well-made arrow can be the difference between a hit and a miss.

Arrows can be equipped by dragging them over the bow in the inventory."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_53651_FirstModifier,Hallowed
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_51816_FirstModifier,Hallowed
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_51816_SecondModifier,Cripple
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/LegitReligious_Enhanced/LegitReligiousItemTable.uexp,,ItemTable_51464_LongDesc,"<LoreItalics>I am a daughter of Luxur, and before I had known fifteen summers I had been led through the temples of Derketo, the dusky goddess, and had been initiated into the mysteries.</> - Xuthal of the Dusk

This sword, suggestively shaped, seems to twist and bend as light plays across the blade. There is a dark ritual, performed naked by the priests and priestesses of Derketa, that involves this blade, a sacrificial victim and necrophilia. 

Derketo it is said, appears in person to lick the blood from the blade.

This is a sacred weapon, imbued with the blessing of a deity. "
