ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2491640_LongDesc,"A Damascus blade blessed by the powers of the corvid God, Qrow. Commission item."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2491640_FirstModifier,Legendary
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2491640_SecondModifier,Weapon
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2491640_ThirdModifier,Cleansing
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2491641_Name,Twinned Dark Star Sabers
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2491641_ShortDesc,"Paired swords, imbued with Empowering Assault & Withering Strikes"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2491641_LongDesc,"An ominous pair of dual swords forged from a rare and corrupted crystal known for its malevolent energies. Legend has it that the corrupted crystals used in the creation of these sabers were tainted by the very essence of malevolence, making them a formidable force against the ancient legendary blade they were designed to counter. The mere touch of the Twin Dark Star Sabers is said to send shivers down the spine, as if the darkness within the blades resonates with the shadows of one's soul. The blades seem to respond to the inner shadows within the wielder, forging an unholy connection between master and weapon. The swords become an extension of the wielder's malevolent intent, and as such, they are both feared and coveted by those who seek power in the realm of shadows. Commissioned by Netherkings_"
