ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2492171_Name,Parrinthean Overseer's Helm
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2492171_ShortDesc,"Heavy headwear, imbued with Empowering Dodge"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2492171_LongDesc,"Often seen being worn by Parith’s elite guards, it’s made of the highest quality metals money can buy, and forged by quality smiths of the Holy See. The decoration and embellishments not only depict a story upon each individual overseers helm, but shows the status and authority one wields. Some stories tell of overseers taking  a shot to the head or faceplate by a musket. Others say they’ve seen their helms crack by taking a simple sword cut. Whether these stories hold water or are mere myth, they leave the majority of Parrith staying in line, following the law. Commissioned by Parry."
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2492171_FirstModifier,Relic
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2492171_SecondModifier,Heavy Armor
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2492171_ThirdModifier,Empowering Dodge
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2492172_Name,Parrinthean Overseer's Ultra Greatsword
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2492172_ShortDesc,"A massive, two handed sword imbued with Empowering Assault & Lacerating Strikes"
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/HighmanesArsenal/HA_ItemTable.uexp,,HA_ItemTable_2492172_LongDesc,"This swords design dates back to the late 3rd age. When Parrinthean was faced with Pirates in the Kaidean gulf. Upon the execution of the pirates leaders atop Parrith’s walls the executioner missed barely with their axe resulting in a sloppy execution. Thus relenting to the design of a much more hefty great sword with no point. With embellished designs on its blade leads it to be almost ceremonial, yet the chance to botch an execution compared to an axe head, was far lower. In present times each member of Parrith’s overseers carry the blade not only for its original use, but to also defend Parrith’s peoples. it’s used often to defend the people, while remaining a stark reminder, of what awaits them should they be found convicted of a heinous enough crime. Commissioned by Parry."
