ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EnhancedArmoryAndArsenal/Datatables/DT_EAA_Itemtable.uexp,,ItemTable_19500_Name,Flesh of Remembrance
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EnhancedArmoryAndArsenal/Datatables/DT_EAA_Itemtable.uexp,,ItemTable_19500_ShortDesc,Flesh which bears remembrance of Jhebbal Sag
ConanSandbox/Content/Mods/EnhancedArmoryAndArsenal/Datatables/DT_EAA_Itemtable.uexp,,ItemTable_19500_LongDesc,"<LoreItalics>Once all living things worshipped him. That was long ago, when beasts and men spoke one language. Men have forgotten him; even the beasts forget. Only a few remember. The men who remember Jhebbal Sag and the beasts who remember are brothers and speak the same tongue.</> - Beyond the Black River

There are very few now who remember Jhebbal Sag and his religions. Primarily in Pictland and the Black Kingdoms is he venerated.

But all men were once worshippers and they shared a language with the beasts of the world. In the midnight grove, a realm that exists purely in the thoughts of the god, a worthy challenger might confront their bestial nature and rather than overcome it, instead learn to be at peace with it.

This flesh awakens the ancient language within a person, restoring the worship of Jhebbal Sag to their hearts."
